  "notes": [
    "DRAFT. Rules were transcribed from the predecessor project's four hard-coded classes plus general German practice – they are a starting point, not a verified source.",
    "Deggendorf household setups observed by the original project: residual and paper bins next to houses, sometimes inside a locked shed; glass only at communal banks, typically near offices or larger buildings.",
    "Glass banks are the known hard case. The predecessor's deck names Glas as 'the biggest problem'. Body colour alone is unreliable because many banks are a uniform green shell with per-aperture colour coding – hence requires_disambiguation on the generic rule until aperture detection lands in v2."
  ]
